{"model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are a Python coding agent. Work in the current directory.\n\n# Task\n\nThere is an infinite 2D plane.\nYou are given a positive integer k. You are also given a 2D array queries, which contains the following queries:\n\nqueries[i] = [x, y]: Build an obstacle at coordinate (x, y) in the plane. It is guaranteed that there is no obstacle at this coordinate when this query is made.\n\nAfter each query, you need to find the distance of the k^th nearest obstacle from the origin.\nReturn an integer array results where results[i] denotes the k^th nearest obstacle after query i, or results[i] == -1 if there are less than k obstacles.\nNote that initially there are no obstacles anywhere.\nThe distance of an obstacle at coordinate (x, y) from the origin is given by |x| + |y|.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: queries = [[1,2],[3,4],[2,3],[-3,0]], k = 2\nOutput: [-1,7,5,3]\nExplanation:\n\nInitially, there are 0 obstacles.\nAfter queries[0], there are less than 2 obstacles.\nAfter queries[1], there are obstacles at distances 3 and 7.\nAfter queries[2], there are obstacles at distances 3, 5, and 7.\nAfter queries[3], there are obstacles at distances 3, 3, 5, and 7.\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: queries = [[5,5],[4,4],[3,3]], k = 1\nOutput: [10,8,6]\nExplanation:\n\nAfter queries[0], there is an obstacle at distance 10.\nAfter queries[1], there are obstacles at distances 8 and 10.\nAfter queries[2], there are obstacles at distances 6, 8, and 10.\n\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= queries.length <= 2 * 10^5\nAll queries[i] are unique.\n-10^9 <= queries[i][0], queries[i][1] <= 10^9\n1 <= k <= 10^5\n\n\u8acb\u5beb\u4e00\u500b\u9802\u5c64 Python \u51fd\u5f0f\uff08\u4e0d\u8981\u7528 class\uff09\uff1a\ndef resultsArray(queries: List[List[int]], k: int):\n\u53ea\u80fd\u7528\u6a19\u6e96\u51fd\u5f0f\u5eab\u3002\u51fd\u5f0f\u5fc5\u9808\u56de\u50b3\u7b54\u6848\uff0c\u4e0d\u8981\u5370\u51fa\u3002\n\n## Entry point\n\nDefine a function named `resultsArray` in a file called `solution.py` in the\ncurrent directory. It must handle the argument types shown in the checks\nbelow.\n\n## Visible acceptance checks\n\nThe following checks are run against `solution.py` when this process exits:\n\n```\n- `resultsArray([[1, 2], [3, 4], [2, 3], [-3, 0]], 2) == [-1, 7, 5, 3]`\n- `resultsArray([[5, 5], [4, 4], [3, 3]], 1) == [10, 8, 6]`\n```\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Write the complete `solution.py` in the current directory.\n- If a file named `VACANT_FEEDBACK.md` exists in the current directory,\n  read it first: it is acceptance feedback from a previous attempt.\n- Do not write any other files.\n\n\nWrite the complete file solution.py in the current directory, defining the required entry-point function.\nReply with the full content of solution.py inside exactly one ```python code block. No prose outside the code block."}], "max_tokens": 32768, "temperature": 0}